AB  - Therapeutic bronchoscopy has come a long way from removal of foreign bodies to 
      minimally invasive techniques in management of diseases like lung cancer, chronic 
      obstructive pulmonary disease and asthma. This article discusses the exciting new 
      techniques of therapeutic bronchoscopy namely; bronchoscopic lung volume 
      reduction, bronchial thermoplasty, radiofrequency ablation, and use of fiducial 
      markers in external beam irradiation.
