TI  - Thermal ablation for asthma: current status and technique.
PG  - S104-S109
LID - 10.21037/jtd.2016.11.113 [doi]
AB  - Bronchial thermoplasty (BT) is a novel technique used in the treatment of severe 
      asthma. A catheter is advanced through the bronchoscope and directed 
      radiofrequency waves are applied to the segmental bronchi to reduce airway smooth 
      muscle mass. Several randomized clinical trials demonstrate improvement in 
      quality of life and reduction in exacerbation rates after treatment. BT is a safe 
      and cost effective treatment option for severe asthma which is refractory to 
      medical treatment. Further studies are needed in order to better describe the 
      mechanism of action and the asthma subphenotype that was best benefit from this 
      treatment.
