TI  - Refractory asthma - beyond step 5, the role of new and emerging adjuvant 
      therapies.
PG  - 69-77
LID - 10.1177/1479972314562210 [doi]
AB  - A small percentage of asthmatics have 'severe refractory asthma', where there is 
      suboptimal response to currently available therapies. A number of novel therapies 
      targeting key biological targets are becoming available. Asthma is a 
      heterogeneous disease, and systematic evaluation of patients is important to 
      target therapies to the underlying inflammatory subtype and clinical features. 
      This review article outlines new and emerging treatments for severe asthma, 
      including monoclonal antibodies targeting eosinophilic disease, anti-neutrophil 
      strategies, novel bronchodilators and bronchial thermoplasty. We highlight the 
      importance of individualized investigation, treatment and management of severe 
      asthmatics.
