VI  - 126
IP  - 5
DP  - 2018 May
TI  - Anesthetic Considerations for Patients Undergoing Bronchial Thermoplasty.
PG  - 1575-1579
LID - 10.1213/ANE.0000000000002425 [doi]
AB  - Bronchial thermoplasty (BT) is a novel, Food and Drug Administration-approved 
      nondrug treatment for patients whose asthma remains uncontrolled despite 
      traditional pharmacotherapy. BT involves application of controlled radiofrequency 
      energy to reduce airway smooth muscle in large- and medium-sized airways. 
      Although BT is often performed under general anesthesia, anesthetic management 
      strategies for BT are poorly described. We describe the anesthetic management of 
      7 patients who underwent 19 BT treatments in a tertiary academic medical center.
